c:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134950224,imgsize-85896.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 1956, Tressa Prisbrey turned discarded bottles into a 15-building folk-art village in California]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134949257.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Tressa Prisbrey, at age 60, began building Bottle Village using glass bottles from a local landfill. Over 25 years, she constructed 15 unique structures dedicated to her lost children and their memories. The site eventually became a cultural landmark and received various recognitions for its artistic significance. Visitors paid small admission fees to see her creative work and hear her story.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1956-a-60-year-old-california-woman-found-building-blocks-too-expensive-and-began-hauling-bottles-from-a-dump-25-years-later-she-had-turned-tens-of-thousands-of-discarded-objects-into-a-15-building-folk-art-village/articleshow/134949257.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1956-a-60-year-old-california-woman-found-building-blocks-too-expensive-and-began-hauling-bottles-from-a-dump-25-years-later-she-had-turned-tens-of-thousands-of-discarded-objects-into-a-15-building-folk-art-village/articleshow/134949257.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-14T23:47:02+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134949499,imgsize-1077014.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Alice Waters’ school garden project grew into a global network of 5,800 programmes across 75 countries]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134947234.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Launched back in 1995 in California, the Edible Schoolyard Project has blossomed into a global initiative founded by chef Alice Waters. The project imparts essential lessons on gardening and environmental stewardship, seamlessly integrating with subjects like science and math. With a mission to foster healthy eating habits, it has inspired educational platforms across more than 75 countries, aiming to weave food education into everyday school curricula for enhanced student wellbeing.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1995-chef-alice-waters-started-the-edible-schoolyard-at-a-berkeley-middle-school-31-years-later-its-network-connects-more-than-5800-food-and-garden-education-programs-across-75-countries/articleshow/134947234.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1995-chef-alice-waters-started-the-edible-schoolyard-at-a-berkeley-middle-school-31-years-later-its-network-connects-more-than-5800-food-and-garden-education-programs-across-75-countries/articleshow/134947234.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-14T23:37:11+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134949179,imgsize-1428502.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US needs 1.7m skilled workers a year, but Trump's visa war risks talent crunch]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134948284.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-needs-1-7-million-skilled-workers-a-year-but-trumps-visa-crackdown-could-leave-industries-short/articleshow/134948284.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-needs-1-7-million-skilled-workers-a-year-but-trumps-visa-crackdown-could-leave-industries-short/articleshow/134948284.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-14T23:18:51+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vijaya Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134948594,imgsize-53344.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Kimberly Guilfoyle will bring down Trump family after her shocking ouster, insiders aware of her 'burn book' fear]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134947874.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/kimberly-guilfoyle-will-bring-down-trump-family-after-her-shocking-ouster-insiders-aware-of-her-burn-book-fear/articleshow/134947874.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/kimberly-guilfoyle-will-bring-down-trump-family-after-her-shocking-ouster-insiders-aware-of-her-burn-book-fear/articleshow/134947874.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-14T22:58:17+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134947893,imgsize-93048.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[New Zealand couple turns old school into a home with a twist]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134920201.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[After acquiring a rundown school in Tokanui, Ian and Sue Rogers dedicated years and around NZ$250,000 to revitalize the property, successfully turning it into a beloved family residence. They maintained many of the school’s original features, which highlight its rich history. They even converted a damaged swimming pool into a delightful chalet. Eager for their next venture, the couple has decided against tackling another school renovation.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/a-new-zealand-couple-bought-an-abandoned-school-then-spent-three-years-and-about-nz250000-turning-the-classroom-into-a-home-and-chalet-the-property-is-now-listed-for-enquiries-over-nz595000/articleshow/134920201.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/a-new-zealand-couple-bought-an-abandoned-school-then-spent-three-years-and-about-nz250000-turning-the-classroom-into-a-home-and-chalet-the-property-is-now-listed-for-enquiries-over-nz595000/articleshow/134920201.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-14T23:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134920322,imgsize-246998.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[London man bought painting for £45 in 1968; it turned out to be a Van Gogh worth up to €15 million]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134915639.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A painting bought for just £45 from a London junk shop in 1968 was later authenticated as an original Vincent van Gogh. The artwork, which had previously sold for only £4 at a farm sale in 1967, changed hands several times before being sold to a private collector for approximately €12 million to €15 million in 2020.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/in-1968-a-london-buyer-paid-45-for-a-painting-in-a-junk-shop-because-he-suspected-it-might-be-special-experts-later-confirmed-it-as-a-van-gogh-and-in-2020-the-work-sold-for-about-12-million-to-15-million/articleshow/134915639.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/in-1968-a-london-buyer-paid-45-for-a-painting-in-a-junk-shop-because-he-suspected-it-might-be-special-experts-later-confirmed-it-as-a-van-gogh-and-in-2020-the-work-sold-for-about-12-million-to-15-million/articleshow/134915639.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-14T23:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134916027,imgsize-150434.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Shania Twain turns childhood hunger into school support for vulnerable children through her charity]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134915848.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Founded in 2010, Shania Twain's Shania Kids Can initiative seeks to empower children facing poverty and food insecurity. The program provides academic help and emotional support in a nurturing school atmosphere, aiming to enhance children's self-esteem, food security, and mental health, all vital for effective learning. With dedicated Clubhouses, the foundation directly engages with children in their everyday setting, steadily reaching out to underserved communities throughout North America.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/shania-twain-went-to-school-hungry-as-a-child-after-launching-shania-kids-can-in-2010-she-helped-bring-school-based-support-to-vulnerable-children-including-a-clubhouse-in-north-las-vegas/articleshow/134915848.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/shania-twain-went-to-school-hungry-as-a-child-after-launching-shania-kids-can-in-2010-she-helped-bring-school-based-support-to-vulnerable-children-including-a-clubhouse-in-north-las-vegas/articleshow/134915848.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-14T22:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134915963,imgsize-94637.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[A judge voided Rhode Island’s seizure of 31 acres planned for 252 affordable homes]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134946332.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A federal judge ruled against the Town of Johnston, asserting the town lacked authority to seize a property. The judge's decision allows the Santoro family to proceed with a 252-unit affordable housing project. The town had attempted to use eminent domain to halt the development, claiming the land was needed for a municipal complex. Legal challenges arose regarding the town’s adherence to proper procedures and public notification.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-rhode-island-family-planned-more-than-200-affordable-apartments-on-31-acres-the-town-seized-the-site-for-a-municipal-complex-after-a-775000-appraisal-but-a-federal-judge-later-voided-the-taking/articleshow/134946332.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-rhode-island-family-planned-more-than-200-affordable-apartments-on-31-acres-the-town-seized-the-site-for-a-municipal-complex-after-a-775000-appraisal-but-a-federal-judge-later-voided-the-taking/articleshow/134946332.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-14T22:19:44+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134946895,imgsize-1245994.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Indian-origin man in Australia denied bail for 'stalking' woman he met on dating app; judge says risk to her safety 'too great']]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134946739.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/indian-origin-man-in-australia-denied-bail-for-stalking-woman-he-met-on-dating-app-judge-says-risk-to-her-safety-too-great/articleshow/134946739.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/indian-origin-man-in-australia-denied-bail-for-stalking-woman-he-met-on-dating-app-judge-says-risk-to-her-safety-too-great/articleshow/134946739.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-14T22:18:24+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Gokul Ankari</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134947153,imgsize-930249.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Cleveland must consider compensation after rezoning a $52,100 used-car lot investment for housing]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134945137.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[An Ohio appellate court has determined that Cleveland owes TMS Enterprises compensation following a contentious zoning amendment. The firm had invested in land with plans for a used-car dealership, but the city reclassified the site from commercial to residential, derailing their business intentions. TMS argued this decision violated their property rights. The court upheld the initial judgment, initiating the steps for formal compensation proceedings.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-ohio-company-paid-12100-for-cleveland-land-and-put-40000-into-a-planned-used-car-lot-months-later-the-city-rezoned-it-residential-and-an-appeals-court-said-the-move-was-a-compensable-taking/articleshow/134945137.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-ohio-company-paid-12100-for-cleveland-land-and-put-40000-into-a-planned-used-car-lot-months-later-the-city-rezoned-it-residential-and-an-appeals-court-said-the-move-was-a-compensable-taking/articleshow/134945137.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-14T21:18:49+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134946292,imgsize-1438385.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[A UK civil servant allegedly earned £349,378 across eight government jobs between 2020 and 2023]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134946022.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A UK civil servant allegedly earned £349,378 across eight government jobs between February 2020 and September 2023. Kashim Chowdhury, 55, reportedly held five full-time roles simultaneously and was contracted to work 183 hours a week. He is accused of fraudulently securing positions at several government departments and denies nine counts of fraud.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-uk-civil-servant-kashim-chowdhury-allegedly-juggled-five-full-time-government-jobs-earned-349378-across-eight-roles-between-2020-and-2023-and-was-contracted-to-work-183-hours-a-week/articleshow/134946022.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-uk-civil-servant-kashim-chowdhury-allegedly-juggled-five-full-time-government-jobs-earned-349378-across-eight-roles-between-2020-and-2023-and-was-contracted-to-work-183-hours-a-week/articleshow/134946022.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-14T21:10:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134946165,imgsize-196100.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Child among 6 killed in small plane crash in Wisconsin; FAA, NTSB probe underway]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134946355.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Six individuals lost their lives, including a child, after a plane crash in Wisconsin Dells. The small Piper P